  "term": "e_piano",
  "says": "The FM electric piano (the DX7 tine): a carrier and a modulator at the same pitch (ratio 1:1, so every sideband is a harmonic), the index high at the strike and falling within a fraction of a second so the note starts bright and metallic and settles to near a sine; a long decay, no sustain, velocity to the index rather than the level. Signature: an instant attack, harmonic, a decay to -20 dB between half a second and three seconds, a brightness that is highest at the onset.",
